SUB pdfPushGraphicsStack
  '_pdf_)
  '_pdf_@F1,14W60L16
  '_pdf_T
  '_pdf_T A well-structured PDF document typically contains many graphical elements that are essentially independent of each other and sometimes nested to multiple levels. The graphics state stack allows these elements to make local changes to the graphics state without disturbing the graphics state of the surrounding environment. The stack is a LIFO (last in, first out) data structure in which the contents of the graphics state can be saved and later restored.
  '_pdf_T
  '_pdf_@F2,14W60L16TParameters
  '_pdf_@F1,14W60L16T
  '_pdf_T   None.
  '_pdf_T
  '_pdf_@F2,14W60L16TReturns
  '_pdf_@F1,14W60L16T
  '_pdf_T   Nothing.
  '_pdf_T
  '_pdf_@F2,14W60L16TExample
  '_pdf_T _________________________________________________________
  '_pdf_@F1,10W80L10T

  DIM AS LONG ub
  ub = UBOUND(pdfCommand)
  pdfCommand(ub).command = PDF_COMM_PUSH_GRAPHIC_STACK
  REDIM _PRESERVE pdfCommand(ub + 1) AS tPDFCOMMAND
END SUB
'_pdf_E+#40,740@F2,14W60L16
'_pdf_(
